<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/normal_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: Chapter 2 &nbsp;(Read 194 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=81" title="View the profile of Phoebie">Phoebie</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 15<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=81"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:brneydmzo@bellsouth.net"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=116.msg371#msg371"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=116.msg371#msg371">Chapter 2</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> April 10, 2003, 01:59:02 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							The high elf winced slightly as he watched the little dwarf wipe the blood off of his blade with disgusting enthusiasm. &nbsp;He had just watched the small paladin wreak havoc on the poor rat, his holy blade slicing through the rodent flesh with deadly accuracy. &nbsp;The rat had screeched and fallen into several steaming pieces after only a few seconds, and now the paladin grinned widely, showing a crooked set of overly-large dwarf teeth surrounded by a wiry brown beard. &nbsp;The young mage would never get used to all the blood and gore that accompanied a raid, and even though his skin had grown thicker after a few months, he still found himself queasy and short of appetite many hours after an adventure. &nbsp;Almost as if to further disgust the mage, the paladin pretended to lick his sword, cackling at the look of horror that crossed Edaar's face.<br /><br />&quot;I'm only joking, mage. Relax, you look like you just saw a ghost. Hahaha...get it? Ghost? In Hate? HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA....&quot;<br /><br />The paladin stumbled off, slapping his knee in amusement, completely entertained by his own bad joke. &nbsp;Koradmer had joined the ranks of Anthology about a year ago, and had quickly established himself as a bit of a wild man when it came to undead monsters. &nbsp;His energy during battle was something that had amazed his comrades at first, for such a tiny little dwarf the power of his swing and fury of his melee was a thing of wonder. &nbsp;He was slightly crazy, and perhaps the fact he was a little left of center may have been what allowed him to commit the somewhat psychotic antics he had become renowned for among his guildmates.<br /><br />Edaar took out his handkerchief, and wiped the slight spatters of rat blood off of his boots. &nbsp;He checked his pet elemental's health, and finding him at full life and on guard, he breathed a sigh of relief. &nbsp;Where were the others, he wondered? 12 people here in Hate had managed so far to hold control, but now that one of their numbers was missing, a somber silence had fallen throughout the ranks as they waited, trapped in their own fear, hoping that reinforcements would arrive soon.<br /><br />The screeching voices of the trapped spirits echoed through the high ceilings and ghastly towering architecture, the ache of their enslavement evident in the hollow screech of their pleading howls. &nbsp;Darkness seemed to lurk around every corner here, death crouching in the spreading shadows, fiends and revenants hiding around every corner, longing to latch onto the souls of the living for some sort of temporary sustinence, something to make them feel alive amidst this barren plane of death. &nbsp;It was dangerous to be surrounded so completely by creatures who had nothing to lose. &nbsp;Life was the enemy here, and it was almost as if the dead things could smell and taste the healthy blood that surged through the veins of the 12 adventurers. &nbsp;Cold breezes randomly swept up the walls, leaving trails of chill bumps across exposed flesh, making hair stand on end, setting jaws on edge. &nbsp;The overall feel of this place was one of confusion and suffocation, even for those of the dark persuasions. &nbsp;Wretched writhing monsters, even more frightening than the creatures summoned up by the most powerful necromancers wriggled across the stone carved ground and across this sprawling enclosed citadel of malevolence and scorn. &nbsp;This was certainly not a place one chose to come to frequently, if ever.<br /><br />The howling of the dead became louder, and the adventurers at once all stood up, knowing that this signaled the arrival of more living things, and it seemed that each alive and healthy person that entered this place fueled the hatred and anger of Innoruuk. &nbsp;The echo of his maniacal laughter crept into one's very soul with icy tendril-like fingers, gripping the heart and squeezing it empty of any courageous resolve that may have remained.<br /><br />&quot;We're here.&quot;<br /><br />Edaar and Aussie jumped at the sound of the voice behind them, everyone seemed on edge and even the slightest surprise was enough to incite a coronary.<br /><br />&quot;Dammit rogue, don't fucking do that,&quot; said Aussie, his profanity a sign of his fear and anger, for he normally kept quiet, summoning his pets to do his dark biddings, his mastery of the necromantic magic usually being all the voice he needed to make his point. &nbsp;Finggaz giggled, always liking to catch people off guard. &nbsp;He had the innate ability to slink into shadows and darkness, making him invisible even to the undead, an ability which would now come in handy as they searched for the missing guildmate. &quot;So, did we hear a rumor someone may have....died?&quot; &nbsp;<br /><br />Aussie stood up immediately, shot a look of death at Finggaz, and snapped his fingers, poofing his pet into a clattering pile of bones. &nbsp;&quot;She is NOT dead, I can still sense her spirit. Bite your tongue, rogue. &nbsp;We WILL find her, she's just...misplaced at the moment. &nbsp;I don't want to hear you say &quot;dead&quot; or &quot;death&quot; again, do you UNDERSTAND?&quot; &nbsp;The dark elf's eyes gleamed with fierce determination, his entire body shaking violently, from fear or frustration, Finggaz could not determine, but he knew at once that the person who was missing had to be the cleric Cinamini, Aussie's wife. &nbsp;He regretted his outburst now, hoping that Aussie knew it was not an intentional attempt to hurt or scare him.<br /><br />&quot;I'm sorry Aussie. I didn't know. &nbsp;Where was she last seen?&quot;<br /><br />Aussie had walked away, sulking, his deep purple robes trailing behind him like a sail, his steps echoing through the cavernous alley between the walls where they had set up a temporary base. &nbsp;<br /><br />&quot;God, if putting your foot in your mouth was a national sport, you'd hold the GOLD MEDAL, man.&quot; &nbsp;<br /><br />Finggaz snapped his head around to see the grimace of the large green troll Lewter, his too-big-to-be-allowed warrior friend. &nbsp;Lewter sat at the base of the corner of the wall, whetting stone in hand, sharpening his blades with fierce fervor. &nbsp;<br /><br />&quot;I mean seriously, Fing... You could have like, asked, before you went shooting your mouth off...for all we know, we may never see Cinamini again.&quot; &nbsp;<br /><br />Lewter returned to his sharpening, and he tossed a loving glance up at the elegant wood elf who stood over him, her lute in her hand, singing a soothing song of restoration for the weary and discouraged ranks of soldiers. &nbsp;Darla was tall, with dark red hair and olive elven skin, her armor a deep maroon color, her smile mischevious and soothing. &nbsp;She patted the shoulder of the troll lovingly, staring at him gently, her love for him evident in her large almond-shaped eyes. &nbsp;The troll breathed a sigh, squeezed her hand briefly, and returned to his task. &nbsp;Perhaps one of the strangest pairings in Norrath, this couple was known for their overwhelmingly adorable displays of public affection, but at this moment, they seemed to cling to one another merely for strength and comfort, all thoughts of romance devoid from their brain for the time being as they undoubtedly worried for the fate of their friend.<br /><br />Eelyen arrived, greeting each guild member with a handshake and a nod of his head, asking them all questions about what had happened. &nbsp;If you looked closely enough at his face, you could almost see the wheels spinning as he began to formulate a strategy of attack and recovery, his mind set on the goal of saving their lost guildmember. &nbsp;Although flighty at times, when given a task to accomplish, Eelyen's strength of purpose and determination to succeed was overwhelming and uplifiting; his ability to encourage and motivate quietly and gently was something that allowed those who followed him to respect and love him unwaveringly.<br /><br />Koradmer rolled back into camp, zipping up his trousers, grinning like the cat who had just swallowed the canary. &nbsp;&quot;Well, if Innoruuk finds that little present I just left in one of his fire pots, I am sure he'll come looking for me straight away! hahahahahahah!&quot;<br /><br />At this moment, a bit of humor was just what people needed to ease the tension, and a ripple of laughter spread through the ranks, easing the minds temporarily and reminding them that they were, if anything, together now, a force of 16, with 2 more on the way soon. &nbsp;18 was certainly better than 12, and perhaps as word spread more Anthology members would begin to arrive, sensing the urgency of the matter.<br /><br />Pyrho sat down next to Lewter, looking at his blades, talking about weaponry. &nbsp;Navenya spotted the pair, and sat down to talk with them as well, the three of them discussing strategies and approaches for the upcoming battle. &nbsp;Their heads pressed together in a tight circle, one would never suspect that they had not known one another for more than a year, for the adventures they had shared this year alone were enough to bond them for life. &nbsp;Once you have saved someone's life to have them save it right back in return, an unspoken loyalty blooms, an affection born out of comraderie and unity of purpose, one that holds true even amidst the most challenging of encounters, each swing of the sword strengthening your friendship, each wound bandaged solidifying a union that is invisible yet indestructible.<br /><br />&quot;Alright everyone, can I please have your attention? It's time to get down to business.&quot;<br /><br />Heads raised up, eyes searching out the face of their leader Eelyen, sharpening stones silencing, spellbooks snapping shut, the circle of friends tightening into a small cluster.<br /><br />&quot;Cinamini is here, we can still sense her, we know she is strong of spirit and soul, and that she has magic that can keep her safe...for awhile. &nbsp;However, we must find her soon, for I can feel the hatred and anger of the Demented One growing stronger with each breath we take. &nbsp;I have a plan of recovery, and if you listen carefully perhaps we can do this quickly and efficiently, with little room for mistake. &nbsp;Finggaz, please find Azeth, wherever he is, and the two of you scout up that spiral ramp and see if you can find a trace of her. &nbsp;Before you do that, please group up with Edaar, so that should you encounter trouble, he can call you back here to safety. &nbsp;Also, if you happen to find Cinamini, the best bet would be to call her back to camp as soon as possible so that if she is hurt or in danger, we can minsiter to her needs quickly. Now go.&quot;<br /><br />Edaar and Finggaz teamed up quickly, and started searching for Azeth. &nbsp;They heard the voice of the rogue from around a dark corner, and approaching him quickly they stopped in their tracks suddenly at what they saw.<br /><br />Azeth was sidled up next to a Forsaken Revenant, looking almost amorously at her as he stared at her pallid flesh and scantily clad body. &nbsp;Her teeth were long and dripping with hot saliva, and she crouched slightly, her shoulders rounded, her hair wild and messy. &nbsp;Strangely enough, she was not attacking him, but merely sat there in the middle of the room, in a trance, completely calm. &nbsp;At once Finggaz knew something was not right. &nbsp;He heard a stifled giggle from the corner behind him, and he suddenly knew what was going on. &nbsp;Hiding in the corner, Dimmal sat, his hands raised in the air, his eyes fixed on the Revenant. <br /><br />&quot;Ssssh, Finggaz, watch.....&quot;<br /><br />Finggaz slipped into the shadows and watched Azeth with growing amusement.<br /><br />&quot;So baby, what's a nice half-naked girl like you doing in a place like this?&quot; &nbsp;Azeth circled the undead woman, eyeing her appreciatively. &nbsp;He reached down and smacked her half-exposed buttocks. &nbsp;&quot;Oh yeah, nice and firm...I like that in a woman, one who can take care of herself and look good for her man...&quot;<br /><br />Finggaz stifled a laugh, and suddenly realized that Dimmal had mezmerized the undead woman, making her temporarily unthreatening. &nbsp;However, Finggaz also knew that at any moment, Dimmal would release her from her trance and she would NOT be happy with the slimy rogue who was now reaching his hand over her shoulder and sliding it down the front of her shirt. &nbsp;&quot;Is he REALLY that dumb?&quot; Finggaz whispered to Dimmal, and Dimmal just nodded and shrugged, shushing Finggaz with a single finger over his mouth. &quot;He's been at this for ten minutes now...I can't bring myself to break the trance, it's too damn funny...&quot; the smile on the enchanter's face grew bigger as Azeth continued hitting on the creature.<br /><br />&quot;Yeah baby, that's right, a woman shouldn't say much, she should just stand there and look good....so, how about you and me go find the Maestro's bedroom and....&quot;<br /><br />CRACK.<br /><br />The revenant snapped out her trance, her eyes suddenly glowing red, her smile spreading widely as she slithered towards Azeth, her hands reaching towards his neck, her fingernails long and glinting with fresh blood from a recent kill.<br /><br />&quot;Uh....um....well....I didn't mean that....uh...&quot; Azeth stumbled towards the corner where Dimmal was hiding, and realizing he had been tricked, Azeth began tossing around a string of profanities that would make even an ogre blush. &nbsp;Finggaz quickly equipped his dagger, and snuck around behind the woman, his Ragebringer sinking deeply into her spiny white back, meeting its mark with a soft sick thud as he sunk it hard to the hilt. &nbsp;She quivered, a look of surprise crossing her face, and poofed into a cloud of smoke, leaving behind merely a shell of flesh on the ground at their feet.<br /><br />&quot;Azeth, you really need to stop thinking with your penis. &nbsp;One of these days, I am NOT going to be here to save your ass,&quot; said Finggaz as he wiped his blade on his trousers and re-equipped it on his right hip scabbard. &nbsp;Dimmal collapsed onto the floor, tremors of laughter overwhelming him. &nbsp;He gasped for air, tried to speak, and finding himself short of breath, merely stopped trying and continued to point and laugh at the rogue. &nbsp;He managed to get a few words out.<br /><br />&quot;Never...thought....you could be so dumb....such a...tard....God...that was too easy.....&quot;<br /><br />Azeth grimaced and stalked off towards camp. &nbsp;&quot;WAIT!&quot; Finggaz cried out. &quot;We have to group up and go look for Cinamini. Join me and Edaar, Eelyen has told us to go check out the situation. Dimmal, get back to camp before that revenant's friends find you and make quick work of your prankster ass. &nbsp;The others are waiting for us, come on Azeth, we must go.&quot; &nbsp;<br /><br />Azeth grudgingly took his invite, and the two rogues stepped into the shadows and began moving up the spiraling ramp, in search of a clue to the whereabouts of the missing cleric.<br /><br />********************<br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg473"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=3" title="View the profile of EQSysquella">EQSysquella</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								GO GO NERFED DPS<br />
								Guild Officer<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
